# Drafted by Gemini (side quests act 2 batch 1: quack), edited.

~ morgan_ask
Narrator: A scrap of herb-stained parchment hangs crookedly from the apothecary door, smelling faintly of crushed mint.
morgan [weary]: If anyone has a spare moment, a pedlar in the Round is selling a plague cure. I cannot leave the kettle, so please see what is in it, and whether it does harm.
* We will look into it -> morgan_accept
* Not now -> END

~ morgan_accept
Narrator: You fold the note into your coat while the pestle keeps up its tired rhythm inside.
quest the_quack asked
set quack_asked
-> END

~ pitch
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: Step lively, good neighbours, and fortify your humours with Pennywhistle's Sovereign Specific. Every green bottle carries a fresh guarantee against the creeping itch, or your brass Cheerfully refunded.
* Ask what is in it -> ask
* Buy a bottle (two gold) -> buy
* Leave -> END

~ ask
barnaby_pennywhistle [sly]: Now, I could hardly hand over my sainted grandmother's receipt in the open damp. Call it forty mountain herbs steeped under a lucky star, and leave the arithmetic to me.
-> pitch

~ buy
gold -2
set quack_bottle
Narrator: The cork gives with a sticky pop, releasing a warm, unmistakable waft of cellar cider and cheap cinnamon.
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: A wise investment for troubled times, friend, and do remember to shake the sediment before supper.
-> pitch

~ verdict
Narrator: Barnaby straightens his cuffs by the crate of clinking bottles, watching the crowd with bright, restless eyes.
* [if flag.quack_bottle] [Nature DC 11] Taste the bottle properly -> id_ok | id_off
* Buy a bottle for two gold -> buy_again
* Press Barnaby for the truth -> press

~ id_ok
Narrator: Beneath the sweet orchard cider and cinnamon bark sits a bitter trace of boiled willow and wildflower honey. It will cure no plague, though it might soothe a feverish throat and warm a cold belly.
set quack_known
-> END

~ id_off
Narrator: The draught burns pleasantly across your tongue with fierce cinnamon and sour apples, masking whatever else might be floating at the bottom.
-> END

~ press
barnaby_pennywhistle [neutral]: You have a terribly solemn look about you, traveller, and solemnity is dreadful for the digestion.
* [Intimidation DC 12] Press Barnaby -> press_ok | press_fail

~ press_ok
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: Keep your voice down, I beg you, before the sick folk lose their temper. It is mulled cider, willow bark for the aches, and a spoonful of honey to keep their spirits from sinking.
set quack_known
-> END

~ press_fail
barnaby_pennywhistle [sly]: Bless your heart, I have faced louder bailiffs in three counties and sold them all hair tonic. Take two bottles for three coins and spare us both the frown.
-> verdict

~ settle
barnaby_pennywhistle [weary]: Well, you have the measure of my little kettle now. A drop of warmth and willow tea is better than cold panic, so what do you mean to do with me?
* Expose him to the village -> expose
* Let him be, but take a bottle for Morgan -> be
* [Persuasion DC 12] Become his partner for a cut -> partner_ok | partner_fail

~ expose
Narrator: Word travels fast around the blankets, and within moments a chorus of coughing townsfolk is pelting Barnaby's cart toward the gate with turnip tops.
barnaby_pennywhistle [afraid]: Ungrateful hamlet, upon my word! May your joints stay draughty and your tea go cold!
set quack_outcome = "exposed"
quest the_quack done
gold +10
-> END

~ be
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: You have a gentle soul beneath that travel dust, friend. Take the best bottle from the bottom row for the apothecary, and take this coin for keeping a quiet tongue.
set quack_outcome = "left"
quest the_quack done
gold +5
-> END

~ partner_ok
barnaby_pennywhistle [sly]: Now there is a head for honest commerce in a dark season. Stand beside the crate looking healthy, nod when I mention the forty herbs, and we shall split the evening's tin.
set quack_outcome = "partner"
quest the_quack done
gold +20
-> END

~ partner_fail
barnaby_pennywhistle [neutral]: No offence meant, my dear colleague, but a trade secret shared with four strangers is just a recipe on a tavern wall.
-> settle

~ buy_again
gold -2
set quack_bottle
Narrator: The bottle smells of cider and cinnamon.
-> verdict
